# Eval-side artifacts. Downloaded / averaged Lightning checkpoints can be
# many GB each and must never be staged for commit (GitHub rejects >100MB
# blobs anyway, and `git add -A` would spend minutes blob-hashing them).
# Same for the per-run scratch dirs the eval driver and HF datasets produce.
checkpoints/
audio_cache/
results/
.tmp_cache/
.mplconfig/

# Local training-curve/comparison plots produced by plot_training_curves.py and
# plot_project_comparison.py. Regenerated on demand from cached logs; never commit.
project_compare*.png
*_comparison.png
*_curves.png

# Eval/validation driver scratch (scripts/speechlm2/run_streaming_stt_training_val.py):
# materialized input wavs, per-run exp_config/manifests, and the multi-MB
# leaderboard manifests. All regenerated on demand — never commit them
# (they bloated sync_to_oci.sh pushes by tens of MB of wav/json blobs).
debug_decode_configs/

# Model artifacts: NeMo/Lightning checkpoints are multi-GB and exceed GitHub's
# 100MB file limit, so they must never be committed (a stray *.nemo once
# bloated a sync push to 2.4GB).
*.nemo
*.ckpt

# Launch scripts that embed personal secrets (HF/WANDB tokens) and per-user
# cluster paths. Kept locally only; rsync to the cluster via the per-dir sync.sh
# instead of git. Covers ord/, ord2/, ord3/, oci/, ... so secrets never get committed.
ord*/
rno/
oci/

# Local-only debug/probe scripts (may reference cluster paths / read tokens from
# env at runtime). Keep out of git so nothing leaks accidentally.
probe_alignment.py

# Hardcoded HF token for the eval wrappers (auto-loaded by eval_leaderboard*.sh).
# NEVER commit: this holds a real Hugging Face access token.
.hf_token
.oci_finish_relaunch.*

# --- Local experiment artifacts (untracked; must not be committed by sync_to_oci.sh git add -A) ---
lora_l2w/
oracle_results/
oracle_results_aishell/
likelihood_results/
